[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: GBSK HVPS Interface Bootloader FW Software Requirements Specification
UID: DHF-GBSK-0021
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: hvps-interface/bootloader

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to provide Software Requirements Specifications for the GBSK HVPS
Interface Bootloader Firmware (FW).
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes all requirements of the GBSK HVPS Interface Bootloader FW.
The information in this document has been derived from the VoxelRay GBSK Product Requirements
Specification, as referenced in this document.

\*The term Software applies to both Software and Firmware systems.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
CRC
  Cyclic Redundancy Check

EC256
  Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm with 256-bit keys

FIH
  Fault Injection Hardening

FW
  Firmware

HVPS
  High Voltage Power Supply

LED
  Light Emitting Diode

MCU
  Microcontroller Unit

PID
  Proportional Integral Derivative controller

PRS
  Product Requirements Specification

RAM
  Random Access Memory

SDP
  Software Development Plan

SRS
  Software Requirements Specification

SW
  Software
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS Interface Bootloader firmware allows the system to be able to update the HVPS Interface
application firmware. The HVPS Interface Bootloader firmware runs on the MCU of the HVPS interface
board.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: References

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
DHF-GBSK-0001, Rev. 1: GBSK Software Development Plan (SDP)

DHF-GBSK-0002: VoxelRay Product Requirements Specification (PRS)
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Functional
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall jump to execution of the HVPS interface application
if and only if the existing application code at startup is valid. The application code is valid if the
programmed CRC value matches the application firmware loaded in flash memory
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Functional
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to write a specified flash memory page with
provided data from the PC.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-3
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Functional
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash
memory, corresponding to the application firmware programming area.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: PC Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to respond to a ping command from the PC,
indicating that the system is in bootloader mode
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-5
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: MCUboot Image Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate application images using the MCUboot bootutil
library, including cryptographic signature verification using EC256 algorithms and verification of
image metadata headers.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-6
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Stack Pointer Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the stack pointer value read from the
application image vector table resides within the valid RAM address range (0x20000000 to 0x20008000)
before jumping to the application.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-7
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Reset Handler Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the reset handler address read from the
application image vector table resides within the valid application code range before jumping to the
application.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-8
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Image Address Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the application image start address falls
within the valid application slot range (0x0800C200 to 0x08024000) before attempting to execute the
application.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
